on  leader boris nemtsov  just before the sixth anniversary of his  death a young man who looks like a  tourist  tells us he's just turned his own life  upside down  yeah i was in the police i resigned when  alexi navalny was sentenced to prison  it takes courage to resign for political  reasons and especially to speak out in  public  but sergey is determined  you can't be scared the whole time boris  nemtsov was not afraid and  neither is alexi navalny it depends on  all of us  every one of us has a stake in the  future of our country  28 old sergey was a police officer for  five years  now he lives on his savings blogging on  youtube and  instagram he posted his resignation  online on the day navalny was convicted  sergey was still wearing the police  uniform  the verdict against navalny was the last  straw  he was also dismayed by the brutal  police crackdown on demonstrations  a police officer kicked a woman to the  ground there were no charges against him  and he wasn't even fired  i don't want to be part of this system  anymore i'm ashamed of the violence even  though i wasn't there  in march sergey traveled to moscow  attending a seminar for local  politicians  organized by civil rights activists  among the speakers prominent opposition  figures  within minutes police stormed the room  they arrest  everyone present including one speaker  we were in the middle of interviewing  of course it's dangerous opposing the  government but this is about russia's  future  sergey himself was arrested for the  first time in his life  he was released and later fined his  former colleagues he says would not  understand his actions  like most in russia they are not  interested in politics just  three cases have been reported of police  officers resigning over the latest  violent unrest  emily you know we saw it there the  kremlin appears to be steadily cracking  down  on the russian opposition is this all  about elections that are taking place in  september  absolutely um i think it seems pretty  clear now that  the kremlin doesn't want any opposition  candidates to even be  allowed to register at least that seems  to be the signal  that we've been getting in the past few  weeks for example there's this  new law which means that anyone uh  deemed to be  extremist or connected with an extremist  organization will be barred from running  in the upcoming elections  that law according to experts seems to  be  squarely aimed at navigating  organizations navain's allies even in  anticipation  of that court verdict that we were  talking about earlier and it's not just  people associated with navalny  for example in the past a few days and  weeks  two prominent opposition figures were  arrested  here in russia andrey pivawarov who was  the coordinator of  open russia a civil society organization  was actually taken out of a plane as he  was trying to fly to warsaw he was  arrested and dmitry gudkov of well-known  opposition politician was also  detained um then released and he has now  left the country he's gone  to ukraine and and we've also been  seeing a crackdown  in other areas not just on politicians  but also on  uh critical media outlets um ngos and  even on  people who took part in protests back in  the winter  and emily what about alexia navalny  himself can you bring us up to date on  his situation  well we know that this week he was  transferred from  a hospital within a prison back to just  a normal  prison he was in hospital because he had  been on hunger strike  doctors called on him to stop his hunger  strike because they said he was close to  dying  he was actually uh protesting the fact  that um  he was not allowed to see independent  doctors even though he was suffering  from symptoms  he said that we're connected with the  fact that he was poisoned  with using a military nerve agent last  year  now it seems that his uh health  condition is stable  and his spirits are up he's been joking  um in letters to his lawyers and uh to  his wife that  um are then posted on instagram uh but  he's still in prison and  seems to it seems that he'll be there  for the upcoming future  emily sherman they're reporting from  moscow thank you  you
 

